  \\ Temporary macro for counting number of # in input using regex conditional
  \\ regex conditional makes it deterministic, which allows it to be run with
  \\ count arguments instead of relying on recursion (f#x based approach)
  \\ Recursion isn't ideal in this case because this is a helper function. 
  \\ Recursive macros rely on failed motions, which not only the terminate 
  \\ the current macro but also the macro which invoked it.
  \\ The max possible # is known (8) so the default/else part of the regex
  \\ conditional can do a no-op when no '#' are present any longer.
  ao
    aa'j
    aa/#
    aax
    aak
  a$v0"0ydd
  a8@0
  a'jj
  a"byl
  a2k4dd
